      "text": "To find the sum of the products of the roots taken two at a time, we use Vieta's formulas. For the polynomial \\(3x^3 - 3x^2 + 11x - 8 = 0\\), the roots are \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\). According to Vieta's formulas, the sum of the products of the roots taken two at a time is given by the coefficient of \\(x\\) (the middle coefficient) divided by the leading coefficient, but with a negative sign. The coefficient of \\(x\\) in the polynomial is 11, and the leading coefficient is 3. Therefore, we have:\n\n\\[\nab + ac + bc = \\frac{\\text{coefficient of } x}{\\text{leading coefficient}} = \\frac{11}{3}\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(ab + ac + bc\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{11}{3}}\\).",
